Excellent. In other words, upstream master already includes the COW corruption fix (the `ctx->current_offset += rdlen;` inside expread, and `pwrite` instead of `write` inside expwrite). Looking at the diff obtained from master, both fixes are already included:

```c
+			if (pread(client->difffile, buf, rdlen, client->difmap[mapcnt]*DIFFPAGESIZE+offset) != rdlen) {
